@anon.984efe779a4077b66be6415f964eeb42.2197 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [794 x i8] }> <{ [794 x i8] c"Cite a work from the bibliography.\0A\0ABefore you starting citing, you need to add a [bibliography] somewhere in\0Ayour document.\0A\0A# Example\0A```example\0AThis was already noted by\0Apirates long ago. @arrgh\0A\0AMultiple sources say ...\0A@arrgh @netwok.\0A\0AYou can also call `cite`\0Aexplicitly. #cite(<arrgh>)\0A\0A#bibliography(\22works.bib\22)\0A```\0A\0AIf your source name contains certain characters such as slashes, which are\0Anot recognized by the `<>` syntax, you can explicitly call `label` instead.\0A\0A```typ\0AComputer Modern is an example of a modernist serif typeface.\0A#cite(label(\22DBLP:books/lib/Knuth86a\22)).\0A>>> #bibliography(\22works.bib\22)\0A```\0A\0A# Syntax\0AThis function indirectly has dedicated syntax. [References]($ref) can be\0Aused to cite works from the bibliography. The label then corresponds to the\0Acitation key." }>, align 1
