@anon.984efe779a4077b66be6415f964eeb42.2257 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [680 x i8] }> <{ [680 x i8] c"The vertices of the path.\0A\0AEach vertex can be defined in 3 ways:\0A\0A- A regular point, as given to the [`line`] or [`polygon`] function.\0A- An array of two points, the first being the vertex and the second\0A  being the control point. The control point is expressed relative to\0A  the vertex and is mirrored to get the second control point. The given\0A  control point is the one that affects the curve coming _into_ this\0A  vertex (even for the first point). The mirrored control point affects\0A  the curve going out of this vertex.\0A- An array of three points, the first being the vertex and the next\0A  being the control points (control point for curves coming in and out,\0A  respectively)." }>, align 1
